(Incident Response and Change Management Protocol) Tj T*
(Document ID: OPS-PRC-004    Version: 1.3    Effective Date: 2026-09-01) Tj T*
(Classification: Internal) Tj T*
T*
(1. Purpose) Tj T*
(This protocol defines the mandatory procedure for responding to production) Tj T*
(incidents and for approving, executing, and rolling back changes to) Tj T*
(production systems.) Tj T*
T*
(2. Severity Classification) Tj T*
(SEV-1: Complete service outage or confirmed data loss. Response within 15) Tj T*
(minutes. All-hands bridge required. Executive notification within 1 hour.) Tj T*
(SEV-2: Major feature unavailable or severe degradation. Response within 1) Tj T*
(hour. On-call engineer plus backup required.) Tj T*
(SEV-3: Minor degradation with workaround available. Response within 4) Tj T*
(business hours. Handled by on-call engineer.) Tj T*
T*
(3. Incident Response Procedure) Tj T*
(Step 1: Detect and acknowledge. The on-call engineer acknowledges the alert) Tj T*
(within the response window and opens an incident ticket.) Tj T*
(Step 2: Triage. Classify severity, identify affected services, and assemble) Tj T*
(the response team. For SEV-1, open the incident bridge immediately.) Tj T*
(Step 3: Mitigate. Prefer rollback or feature-flag disablement over forward) Tj T*
(fixes during active user impact. All mitigation actions are logged in the) Tj T*
(incident ticket with timestamps.) Tj T*
(Step 4: Resolve and verify. Confirm restoration via monitoring and) Tj T*
(customer-facing checks before closing the incident.) Tj T*
(Step 5: Post-mortem. For SEV-1 and SEV-2, a blameless post-mortem is due) Tj T*
(within 5 business days, covering timeline, root cause, and action items.) Tj T*
T*
(4. Change Management Protocol) Tj T*
(All production changes require a reviewed pull request, passing CI, and) Tj T*
(an approved change ticket. Changes are deployed during approved windows) Tj T*
(only, except emergency fixes for SEV-1/SEV-2, which require on-call) Tj T*
(manager approval and a retrospective review the next business day.) Tj T*
T*
(5. Rollback Protocol) Tj T*
(Every deployment must have a tested rollback path. Rollback is initiated) Tj T*
(automatically if error rates exceed 2x baseline for 10 minutes post-deploy,) Tj T*
(or manually by the deploying engineer or on-call manager.) Tj T*
T*
(6. Communication) Tj T*
(SEV-1: status page update every 30 minutes. SEV-2: hourly updates. All) Tj T*
(incident communications are coordinated by the incident commander;) Tj T*
(engineers do not communicate directly with customers during an incident.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
